 price Ager around 60-64% while most raters call it a Tossup", "Thin, dated polling — one September PPP (D-sponsored) poll showing Ager +3"], "rationale": "The fundamentals favor Republicans in an R+5 open seat, but Ager's fundraising advantage, the absence of incumbent Edwards, and markets pricing him near 60-64% tilt the race narrowly Democratic. Most expert ratings call it a Tossup, so a modest Democratic edge with wide uncertainty fits the evidence.", "watch": "Fresh independent polls or a shift in the national environment toward either party could move this tossup district several points in either direction.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Chuck Edwards (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "This western North Carolina open seat sits on Republican-leaning terrain, but incumbent Chuck Edwards is not on the ballot, removing a structural advantage for the GOP. Democrat Jamie Ager has raised over $3 million and holds a large cash advantage, while Republican Jennifer Balkcom's fundraising figures are not reported and outside spending has so far favored Ager modestly.\n\nMost expert raters call the race a Tossup, with one rating it Lean R and another Lean D for a flip. The only recent poll, a Democratic-sponsored September survey, showed Ager up three points, though polling here is thin and older than ideal. Prediction markets put Ager's chances around 60-64 percent, pointing to a narrow Democratic edge in a genuinely competitive race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5972, "margin": 1.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6249, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6236, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6239, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5922, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.5614, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6011, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6565, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.6466, "margin": 2.0}, {"